        "locale": "quy",
        "key": "formats22_page_preview",
        "english": "Selected page preview",
        "proposed": "Akllasqa rapipa ñawpaq rikuchikuynin",
        "decision": "accept",
        "final_value": "Akllasqa rapipa ñawpaq rikuchikuynin",
        "rationale": "Aklla-sqa is the selected-result modifier, not an imperative. It modifies rapi before rapi-pa closes the page possessor phrase; ñawpaq then modifies the possessed presentation, not rapi. Rikuchikuy is the nominal presentation/showing expression, with support -ni- before third-person possessive -n. The balanced [selected page]-pa [preliminary display]-nin construction is grammatical and preserves the complete referent. Ñawpaq has before/front/previous senses elsewhere, but here the preliminary presentation reading is supported by the visual-display noun and chooser context; it does not tell the user to view the preceding page. This is a descriptive noun phrase with no tense, success or loading claim.",
        "confidence": "moderate; bounded independent original-composition review",
